; Nemoviz Book Reader
;
; Translated by:            Claude (Anthropic), 2026
; Verified and modified by: 
;
; Human translators: write your name and the year after the colon above.
; If somebody has signed there already, add another line like theirs
; underneath - every one of them is kept when this file is reordered.
;
; NOTE: MUCH OF THIS VOCABULARY IS COINED, and you should know that before
; you trust it. Ancient Greek has no attested word for a sound card, a cloud
; voice, an API key or an MP3, so where the language ran out the terms here
; were made rather than found: pinakion tou echou, phonai tou nephous, kleis
; API, chronometron. Where a real word existed it was used - bibliotheke,
; kephalaion, selis, phone - and product names are left alone.
; The orthography is polytonic throughout. So this file is usable Greek and
; it is not attested usage. Correct it freely; nothing here rests on a source.
;
; Translate what stands to the RIGHT of the equals sign, and nothing else.
; Anything in braces - {0}, {1} - is filled in by the program and has to
; survive. The two characters \n mean a line break and \n\n a blank line;
; never break a line with a real Enter, because everything after it is
; thrown away when the file is read.
;
; The order is the same in every language and is set in
; tools/lang-order.txt. It follows the program as it is used: the player
; and its panel, then window by window, and inside a window the thing
; itself before the dialogs it opens.

